{"id":"n-20261014-644ek3","category":"gaming","display_title":"K/DA Social Accounts Reactivated","display_title_he":"החשבונות החברתיים של K/DA הופעלו מחדש","short_summary":"Virtual K-pop group K/DA has updated its social media channels after a six-year hiatus, prompting widespread speculation among fans regarding a potential musical comeback.","english_level":"C1","words":421,"reading_time":3,"image":null,"sources":[{"name":"IGN","domain":"ign.com","url":"https://www.ign.com/articles/kda-reactivates-social-accounts-fueling-rumors-of-the-virtual-k-pop-groups-comeback","title":"K/DA Reactivates Social Accounts, Fueling Rumors of the Virtual K-Pop Group’s Comeback After 6 Years","published_at":"2026-10-13T19:45:50.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-13T19:45:50.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-14T06:18:19.032Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":9,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["The virtual K-pop phenomenon K/DA has recently revitalized its official social media channels for the first time in six years, instantly igniting fervent speculation across the gaming and music communities regarding a long-awaited comeback. According to reports, the reactivated profiles have entirely wiped their previous posts, replacing them with updated banner and profile graphics. While retaining promotional artwork from the All Out era, the refreshed visuals notably incorporate vibrant hot pink and magenta flames alongside the original lineup of League of Legends champions, which includes Ahri, Akali, Evelynn, and Kai'Sa, as well as the era's guest artist Seraphine.","Originally launched by Riot Games at the 2018 League of Legends World Championship, the virtual girl group achieved massive mainstream success. Their debut single, titled POP/STARS, made history in 2022 by becoming the first K-pop song by a girl group to earn RIAA Platinum certification. This early triumph led to the release of a full EP, entitled All Out, in 2020. Following that release, however, the project largely went dark, leaving fans with only in-game character skins rather than new tracks or live performances.","Speculation about a potential return extends far beyond mere social media refreshes. Earlier this year, datamined leaks from a Wild Rift update first spotted by SkinSpotlights pointed toward a prospective Firestarter skin concept, while users also discovered a newly registered song on the ASCAP Repertory. Meanwhile, other online observers suggested the purple smoke imagery might hint at a crossover event with Fortnite, which has utilized similarly colored aesthetics for its ongoing Fortnitemares event.","Whether a true reunion materializes depends heavily on the scheduling and availability of the international pop stars who voice the virtual characters, namely Madison Beer, Soyeon, Miyeon, and Jaira Burns. Online fan accounts recently began circulating rumors regarding Madison Beer potentially leaving the group. Addressing these rumors during her recent Locket tour, Madison Beer expressed enthusiasm about rejoining the project, noting that while she would love to participate, the decision rests entirely outside her hands. She added that there actually was a conversation a few years ago about doing something again, though she does not know what ultimately happened to it.","As of October 13, Riot Games has offered no official confirmation concerning a K/DA revival, let alone revealing who the group currently includes. Nevertheless, with the League of Legends World Championship tournament currently underway across the United States and the Grand Final scheduled for November 14, observant fans remain hopeful that additional announcements might surface during the prominent tournament where the virtual group first captured global attention."],"facts":[{"fact":"Official K/DA social media accounts updated for the first time in six years, featuring new profile and banner images with hot pink flames and wiped posts.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"K/DA debuted at the 2018 League of Legends World Championship and consists of four virtual champions voiced by Madison Beer, Soyeon, Miyeon, and Jaira Burns.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"The group's single POP/STARS received RIAA Platinum certification in 2022, followed by the All Out EP in 2020.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Datamined leaks from earlier this year pointed to a Firestarter skin concept and a new song registered on the ASCAP Repertory.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Madison Beer stated during her Locket tour that she would love to return to K/DA, though it is not entirely up to her.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Riot has not confirmed any rumors regarding a K/DA comeback.","sources":[1]}],"glossary":[{"text":"virtual","lemma":"virtual","pos":"adj","he":"וירטואלי","name":false},{"text":"phenomenon","lemma":"phenomenon","pos":"n","he":"תופאה","name":false},{"text":"recently","lemma":"recently","pos":"adv","he":"לאודר הזמן האחרון","name":false},{"text":"revitalized","lemma":"revitalize","pos":"v","he":"החיה מחדש","name":false},{"text":"official","lemma":"official","pos":"adj","he":"רשמי","name":false},{"text":"social media","lemma":"social media","pos":"n","he":"מדיה חברתית","name":false},{"text":"channels","lemma":"channel","pos":"n","he":"ערוצים","name":false},{"text":"first time","lemma":"first time","pos":"n","he":"פעם ראשונה","name":false},{"text":"six years","lemma":"six year","pos":"n","he":"שש שנים","name":false},{"text":"instantly","lemma":"instantly","pos":"adv","he":"מידית","name":false},{"text":"igniting","lemma":"ignite","pos":"v","he":"היעת, הצית","name":false},{"text":"fervent","lemma":"fervent","pos":"adj","he":"נוקש, סוער","name":false},{"text":"speculation","lemma":"speculation","pos":"n","he":"השערה","name":false},{"text":"gaming","lemma":"gaming","pos":"n","he":"גיימינג","name":false},{"text":"music","lemma":"music","pos":"n","he":"מוזיקה","name":false},{"text":"communities","lemma":"community","pos":"n","he":"קהליות","name":false},{"text":"reg